WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.149
Searching a word list means comparing the query with every word.

00:06.149 --> 00:14.700
“car”, “cat” and “cart” all start the same, so the same letters get read again and again.

00:15.000 --> 00:21.648
A trie stores each shared beginning once.

00:21.648 --> 00:31.700
“car” and “cat” share c-a, then branch only where they differ.

00:32.000 --> 00:38.742
Inserting reuses every node already there and marks where a word ends.

00:38.742 --> 00:47.700
Looking up “ca” walks c, then a, but no word ends there: search says no, startsWith says yes.

00:48.000 --> 00:56.681
Each operation costs one hop per letter: O(L).

00:56.681 --> 00:59.700
That’s the trie.
